$21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["Brookfield Asset Management Inc is a large-cap financial services business with a $85.6B market cap on $4.8B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 47% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 36-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 43 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.88\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 35\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 100% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9998724239278101},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 33% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (BAM) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_BAM_Movement_112026121201_1795151521.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795151521.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BAM Capital Ranks No. 3 Among Indiana's Largest Private Equity Firms","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/bam-capital-ranks-no-3-among-indianas-largest-private-equity-firms-302942865.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795008720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Goldman Sachs Sees 52 More GW of Data Center Power in 2028. These 3 Stocks Look Best Positioned to Cash In.","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.